  <title>3.4.1: Comparing Scatter Plots with Linear and Nonlinear Trends</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00754</md:content-id>
    <md:title>3.4.1: Comparing Scatter Plots with Linear and Nonlinear Trends</md:title>
    <md:uuid>926e2a4d-d6ff-403a-982c-3fd495c12240</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para dir="ltr">Which one doesn’t belong?</para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para dir="ltr">A. <figure><media alt="Graph of a scatter plot, origin O. distance (miles) and cost (dollars)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5959697fc92170c85eef914973c27cd908475ac8"/></media></figure></para>
    <para dir="ltr">B. <figure><media alt="Graph of a scatter plot, origin O, with grid. Height (millimeters) and weight (milligrams)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a2cffe2402ce74466cff9ac61ce61ebe2133f218"/></media></figure></para>
    <para dir="ltr">C. <figure><media alt="A scatterplot."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/de0a019009ffffea916b212daa4e99a1b8c71862"/></media></figure></para>
    <para dir="ltr">D. <figure><media alt="A scatterplot."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/7981e8f73d76b2015dc8fe4a4d381ec74beaca4e"/></media></figure></para>
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some samples.</para>
    <para>A doesn’t belong because it is the only scatter plot with data that fit a line well and are increasing.</para>
    <para>B doesn’t belong because it is the only scatter plot with data that would not fit a line well and do not show a pattern. </para>
    <para>C doesn’t belong because it is the only scatter plot with data that would fit a line well and are decreasing.</para>
    <para>D doesn’t belong because it is the only scatter plot with data that would not fit a line well and do show a curved pattern. </para>
    
     
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
